<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>☁️ LIVE CLOUD COVER</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/cloud_cover_na/legend.png?v=cloudIR-GOES-18-20261016T1430-GOES-19-20261016T1430-HIMAWARI-9-20261016T1400-METEOSAT-FES-20261016T1345-METEOSAT-IODC-20261016T1345-VIIRS-2026-10-16-2026-10-16-v6" width="600" alt="legend"><br>White = cloud tops (multi-satellite infrared, day + night); transparent = clear sky or no satellite coverage. Infrared brightness, not a cloud-cover percentage.</p><p><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT IR OBSERVATION (multi-satellite, honest timestamps)</p><p><b>Source:</b> GOES-19/18 ABI infrared + Himawari-9 infrared (via NASA GIBS) + Meteosat SEVIRI infrared imagery (via EUMETSAT EUMETView) + VIIRS daily polar supplement (via NASA GIBS)<br/><a href="https://www.goes.noaa.gov/">https://www.goes.noaa.gov/</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p><p><b>Coverage</b> — one at a time, switched right here in this folder:<br>◉ <b>Global Coverage</b> (shown)<br>○ Continental Coverage<br>○ Great Lakes Basin Coverage<br>Pro switches exclusively. Web/app: check exactly one box.</p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE CLOUD COVER</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/cloud_cover_na/legend.png?v=cloudIR-GOES-18-20261016T1430-GOES-19-20261016T1430-HIMAWARI-9-20261016T1400-METEOSAT-FES-20261016T1345-METEOSAT-IODC-20261016T1345-VIIRS-2026-10-16-2026-10-16-v6" width="600" alt="legend"><br>White = cloud tops (multi-satellite infrared, day + night); transparent = clear sky or no satellite coverage. Infrared brightness, not a cloud-cover percentage.</p><p><b>Coverage:</b> Global Coverage<br><b>Observed:</b> 2026-10-16 14:30 UTC<br><b>Provenance:</b> GOES-19 2026-10-16 14:30 UTC; GOES-18 2026-10-16 14:30 UTC; HIMAWARI-9 2026-10-16 14:00 UTC; METEOSAT-FES 2026-10-16 13:45 UTC; METEOSAT-IODC 2026-10-16 13:45 UTC; VIIRS 2026-10-16 00:00 UTC</p><p><b>Coverage</b> — one at a time, switched right here in this folder:<br>◉ <b>Global Coverage</b> (shown)<br>○ Continental Coverage<br>○ Great Lakes Basin Coverage<br>Pro switches exclusively. Web/app: check exactly one box.</p>]]></description>
      <Style>
        <ListStyle>
          <listItemType>radioFolder</listItemType>
        </ListStyle>
      </Style>
      <GroundOverlay>
        <name>Global Coverage</name>
        <visibility>1</visibility>
        <drawOrder>10</drawOrder>
        <Icon>
          <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/cloud_cover_na/current.png?v=cloudIR-GOES-18-20261016T1430-GOES-19-20261016T1430-HIMAWARI-9-20261016T1400-METEOSAT-FES-20261016T1345-METEOSAT-IODC-20261016T1345-VIIRS-2026-10-16-2026-10-16-v6</href>
          <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
          <refreshInterval>300</refreshInterval>
        </Icon>
        <LatLonBox>
          <north>90.0</north>
          <south>-90.0</south>
          <east>180.0</east>
          <west>-180.0</west>
        </LatLonBox>
      </GroundOverlay>
      <GroundOverlay>
        <name>Continental Coverage</name>
